cff-version: 1.2.0
title: kimodo-ggml (vendored subset)
message: >-
  If you use this code, cite kimodo-ggml and NVIDIA Kimodo.
abstract: >-
  Kimodo text-to-motion on ggml, for interactor-motion-guest's motion.elf (RFD 2277 A2): the
  two-stage motion denoiser (denoiser.cpp), the cosine schedule, DDIM step and
  separated CFG (diffusion.cpp), the global-to-local root conditioning
  (motion_rep.cpp), the skeleton tables (skeleton.hpp) and the weights class
  interface (ggml_weights.hpp), from src/, UNMODIFIED. motion_decode.cpp is
  kept for reference; motion.elf decodes with guest/motion/kimodo_decode.h
  instead, the same arithmetic ending in matrices (AGENTS.md rule 11), not
  quaternions. Local adaptations live outside this directory: ggml_weights.cpp
  (fopen, and the Vulkan/CUDA/CPU backend choice) is replaced by
  guest/motion/kimodo_weights.cpp (metadata by the pump's READ, tensors by its
  UPLOAD into the ggml-rd RenderingDevice buffer); the initial noise is drawn
  by guest/motion/noise.h instead of std::normal_distribution (whose output
  differs between standard libraries); the LLM2Vec text encoder and the C API
  are left out of motion.elf (the text encoder is the host's stand-in). The
  host-only files tools/motion_native compiles, src/ggml_weights.cpp,
  src/gguf.cpp, src/gguf.hpp, src/llm_text_encoder.cpp,
  src/llm_text_encoder.hpp, src/llm_tokenizer.cpp, src/llm_tokenizer.hpp,
  include/kimodo/kimodo.hpp and include/kimodo/kimodo_capi.h, are copied from
  the same commit, unmodified, and never enter motion.elf.
  The weights are chibifire/Kimodo-SOMA-RP-v1.1-gguf (tools/models/manifest.tsv).
authors:
  - name: V-Sekai-fire
  - name: NVIDIA (Kimodo, the model and its Python reference)
repository-code: https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/kimodo-ggml
